Sure! Here are the steps:

Import TextMeshPro from the Package Manager
Add a TMP_InputField to your scene
Adjust the size of the field as desired
That's it! The TMP_InputField will automatically show scrollbars when the text exceeds the bounds.

You can also customize various aspects of the scrollbars via the scrollSensitivity, verticalScrollbar, and horizontalScrollbar properties.

So altogether, it might look something like:
```csharp
using TMPro;

public class Example : MonoBehaviour
{
    public TMP_InputField inputField;

    void Start()
    {
        inputField.text = "Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet..."; // Long text to trigger scrollbars
        inputField.fontSize = 20;
        inputField.width = 200; // Adjust size
    }
}
```
